# The build without cross-language link-time optimisation, appended to mozconfig by
# build_nulavio.sh when NULAVIO_MOZCONFIG_EXTRA=mozconfig.no-lto. For a machine that
# cannot fit the release build's link (the build laptop is capped at 16 GiB and 2
# processors) and for trying a change to the engine quickly. Never packaged or
# published (rehearse_release.sh refuses a variant): it is slower than a release.
# It is the build as it was before #364: no C++ LTO, and thin Rust LTO in place of
# the release default's fat pass over gkrust, which needed more than 17 GiB
# (docs/research/evidence/release-rehearsal-2026-11-04.md). The build system appends
# CARGO_RUSTCFLAGS after its own -Clto and rustc keeps the last value; only "export"
# lines reach the makefiles that run Cargo.
ac_add_options --disable-lto
mk_add_options "export CARGO_RUSTCFLAGS=-Clto=thin"
